.TH PATH_JOIN 3
.SH NAME
path_join \- concatenate two path components
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "char* path_join(const char* " a ", const char* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_join
concatenates two path components,
.I a
and
.I b
, ensuring that a system-specific path separator is inserted if necessary.
.PP
The function internally uses a
.B stralloc
to perform the concatenation. If
.I a
does not already end with a path separator, one is automatically inserted before
.I b
is appended.
.PP
The resulting string is null-terminated and dynamically allocated. The caller is responsible for freeing the returned memory when it is no longer needed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to a null-terminated string containing the joined path, or NULL if memory allocation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_append (3),
.BR stralloc (3)